Body:
> Yeah I had to change my opencode.json manually to get all variants. Should be there per default if the provider exists

Thank you! I didn't know this was possible until I read this thread. For anyone else that ran into this, here's how to add to your `opencode.json` file:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "model": "github-copilot/gpt-5.2-codex",
  "provider": {
    "github-copilot": {
      "models": {
        "gpt-5.2-codex": {
          "variants": {
            "xhigh": {
              "reasoningEffort": "xhigh"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

I have a similar issue using both `1.1.28` and `1.1.32`.

I am not getting back any arguments though. I'm getting back their literal placeholders.

```
{
    "method": "prompts/get",
    "params": {
        "name": "tellJoke",
        "arguments": {
            "cats": "$1"
        }
    },
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 5
}
```

Would it be better to compact based on context percentage threshold instead of token count threshold? Or could provide an option?

For example:
```
{
  "compaction": {
    "auto": true,
    "prune": true,
    "token_threshold": 50000  // Trigger compaction when input tokens exceed this value
    "context_threshold": 0.75  // Trigger compaction when context exceeds 75%
  }
}
```

Could auto-compact whenever either of the conditions is met.

I have the same requirement. my case is that a large model needs to understand an image based on a URL.

The prompt is as follows:
https://xxxxx/xxx.png please describe this image.

Opencode interprets the request to the large model as a text:
```json
"messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "https://xxxxx/xxx.png please describe this image",
        }
      ]
```

but the format required for large models is as follows:
```json
    "messages": [
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content":
            [
                {
                    "type": "image_url",
                   "image_url": "https://xxxxx/xxx.png"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "please describe this image"
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
```
I need a hook that can modify messages before making a request to the large model.
